From f64e77607ecc7ec7d4a6d531584965a6d09fa1b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:11:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boss, news: Deliver SpotPass notifications to the HOME Menu

SpotPass files can carry a notification for the NEWS module
(0004013000003502), e.g. Mii Plaza's "Puzzle Swap" and "Mii Force"
announcements. Since 0030 those were skipped.

- BOSS queues such payloads in its system savedata (/news/), also when
  the game has no SpotPass storage. Each NsData ID + version is
  delivered once, so downloading the same file again doesn't bring a
  deleted notification back.
- news:s GetTotalArrivedNotifications returns the queued count;
  SyncArrivedNotifications and SyncOneArrivedNotification (0x0010) add
  them to news.db with their title, message, link and image, the
  arrival time, the SpotPass flag and NsData ID/version, and set the
  unread flag for the HOME Menu.
- Payload layout (confirmed with Mii Plaza's 0x88D and 0x962E):
  0x00 first 0x20 bytes of the notification header (flags, program ID
  to jump to), 0x20 title (UTF-16, 0x40), 0x60 message (UTF-16, fixed
  0x1780 bytes, link after the text), 0x17E0 image when flagged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
